## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical implementation of per-tenant isolation in a shared GCP project, focusing on real-world controls rather than theory.

## Key Concepts
- IAM Conditions and least-privilege service accounts
- VPC Service Controls and Private Service Connect
- Customer-managed encryption keys (CMEK)
- CI/CD gates with synthetic tenants and rollback safety
- Data Loss Prevention (DLP) and ongoing IAM reviews

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo snippet: enforce tenant-scoped sink bindings
const sink = getSink("bigquery-export");
bindPolicy(sink, {
  condition: {
    title: "tenant_scope",
    expression: 'resource.name.startsWith("projects/PROJ/datasets/tenant-")'
  },
  bindings: [{ role: "roles/bigquery.dataEditor", members: ["serviceAccount:tenant-a-sa@proj.iam.gserviceaccount.com"] }]
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt the controls for a new tenant with stricter data residency requirements?
- How would you measure and report control effectiveness to audits?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical containment design across IAM, network perimeters, key management, and rollback validation using synthetic tenants.

## Key Concepts
- IAM conditions for tenant isolation
- Perimeter controls: PSC/VC and VPC Service Controls
- CMEK rotation and data-key isolation
- Automated rollback with synthetic tenants and validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: conditional binding to isolate tenant access
const policy = { bindings: [] };
policy.bindings.push({
  role: "roles/storage.objectViewer",
  members: ["user:tenant-a@example.com"],
  condition: {
    title: "Tenant Access Restriction",
    description: "Restrict access to tenant-specific resources",
    expression: "resource.name.startsWith('projects/_/buckets/tenant-a-')"
  }
});
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical, concrete incident response steps for a multi-tenant GCP SaaS, focusing on rapid containment, credential revocation, and rollback with auditable forensics.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation and containment
- Workload Identity and bindings management
- Network controls: NetworkPolicy, Private Service Connect, VPC Service Controls
- Forensics preservation and rollback playbooks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: containment workflow
const onExfiltration = () => {
  isolateTenant();
  revokeIdentity();
  blockEgress();
  preserveForensics();
  runSyntheticTests();
  rollbackIfNeeded();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the rollback playbook in CI/CD?
- What telemetry confirms containment success?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests end-to-end thinking for tenant-scoped data retention across multiple services with auditability and rollback capabilities.

## Key Concepts

- Data tagging and lineage across Storage, BigQuery, and Pub/Sub
- Tenant-scoped retention policies, TTLs, and legal holds
- IAM Conditions, per-tenant service accounts, and KMS constraints
- Immutable logs and cryptographic attestations for verification
- Rollback procedures and audit verification planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code for tenant deletion
function deleteTenant(tenantId) {
  purgePubSub(tenantId);
  deleteStorageObjects(tenantId);
  dropBigQueryPartitions(tenantId);
  verifyDeletion(tenantId);
  generateAuditReport(tenantId);
}
